description:
**Research Analyst** 










**Do you want to be part of a bold and ambitious team that helps organizations make better decisions with good data?** 










**About The Role** 




 Data Sciences is looking for a research analyst to assist in the development and execution of market research studies, online experiments and other research projects. This is an entry\\-level position for someone who has experience in R. The right fit is someone who is a highly motivated self\\-learner looking to grow and take on a challenging role at a fast\\-growing company. 










**Key Responsibilities** 




 To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform the following satisfactorily:



* Analyzing and visualizing data to identify meaningful patterns and communicate findings through clear, accurate, and visually polished charts, tables, and other deliverables.
* Online survey programming and fielding, including survey setup, testing, quotas, vendor coordination, quality checks, and troubleshooting.
* Establishing research strategies and writing survey questionnaires that align with client objectives and support a clear analytical story, with attention to survey length and respondent experience.
* Drafting and presenting research reports and memos that synthesize findings into clear, accurate, and actionable insights.
* Identify opportunities to streamline workflows, strengthen QA, and solve problems through automation, AI tools, and API integrations.
* Carry out other special projects as required.









**Candidate Qualifications** 




**Education/Experience:** 



* Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field with experience in quantitative methods.
* R programming capabilities: 2\\+ years intermediate experience, with practical experience using the tidyverse (especially dplyr and purrr), writing reusable and modular code, and developing or maintaining R packages.
* Knowledge of version control systems (e.g. git).
* Excellent analytical, communication and writing skills.
* Ability to design clear, compelling, and visually polished data visualizations for technical and non\\-technical audiences.
* Ability to work with code and follow coding best practices.
* Understanding of statistical principles, particularly with respect to survey design and interpretation.
* Exceptionally strong organizational skills: detail\\-oriented, ability to manage several tasks at once and stick to deadlines, good at identifying priorities and managing expectations.
* Flexibility: you don’t get flustered when new challenges are thrown your way.
* Ability to work in a fast\\-paced environment and pivot/react quickly when needed.









**Assets:** 



* Experience in market and/or public opinion research.
* Knowledge of other programming languages and tools (e.g., SQL, Python, JavaScript, Google Apps Script), additional analytics related software development experience is a plus.
* Experience programming, launching, and monitoring surveys programmed in Qualtrics and/or similar survey platforms.
* Familiarity with AWS\\-based data workflows, including storing, querying, transforming, and automating data using tools such as S3, Redshift, DynamoDB, and Lambda.
* Experience safely leveraging LLMs into workflows, especially code assist tools (e.g., Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI), and willingness to integrate new technologies into your work.
* Experience with web development tools like React, Next.js, and modern CSS.
* Experience related to politics or campaigning.
* Experience with public speaking and presenting research to diverse audiences.
* Bilingual in English and French.
* We work globally! Knowledge of other languages is appreciated.









**What We Offer** 



* 100% employer\\-paid competitive health package, including Medical \\& Dental benefits.
* Perkopolis: a free program with discounts and savings on entertainment, hotels, travel, shopping and health and wellness products.
* Hybrid work, both remote and in the office.
* Our Head Office in Montreal always has a supply of snacks and coffee.
* Many internal traditions to create an inclusive and fun environment.
* A MacBook computer on your first day.
* 3 weeks of vacation.
* 5 personal days to use at your discretion.
* A fast\\-paced work environment where every day is different.
* The opportunity for professional development through funded courses, conferences and certifications.
* A startup office space and the opportunity to join a growing, multidisciplinary team.









 Knowledge of English is required for this position, as the incumbent will be required to communicate daily, both orally and in writing, with a predominantly English\\-speaking clientele outside of Quebec.
















**Analyste de recherche** 










 Voulez\\-vous faire partie d'une équipe audacieuse et ambitieuse qui aide les organisations à prendre de meilleures décisions grâce à de bonnes données ?










**Description du poste** 




 Data Sciences recherche une ou un analyste de recherche pour participer au développement et à l’exécution d’études de marché, d’expériences en ligne et d’autres projets de recherche. Il s’agit d’un poste junior pour une personne qui a de l’expérience à programmer avec R. La personne idéale est autodidacte et très motivée. Elle cherche à se développer et à assumer un rôle stimulant au sein d’une entreprise en plein essor.










**﻿Responsabilités** 




 Pour accomplir ce travail avec succès, une personne doit être en mesure d'accomplir les tâches suivantes de manière satisfaisante :









* Analyser et visualiser les données afin d’en dégager des tendances significatives et de communiquer les résultats au moyen de graphiques, de tableaux et d’autres livrables clairs, exacts et soignés sur le plan visuel;
* Programmation et déploiement de sondages en ligne, incluant la configuration, les tests, les quotas, la coordination avec les fournisseurs, les contrôles qualité et le dépannage;
* Établir des stratégies de recherche et rédiger des questionnaires de sondage qui s’harmonisent avec les objectifs des clients et soutiennent une histoire analytique claire, en portant attention à la longueur du sondage et à l’expérience du répondant;
* Rédiger et présenter des rapports de recherche et des mémos qui synthétisent les résultats en analyses claires, exactes et exploitables;
* Repérer des occasions de rationaliser les processus, de renforcer le contrôle qualité et de résoudre des problèmes au moyen de l’automatisation, des outils d’IA et des intégrations d’API;
* Réaliser d'autres projets spéciaux en fonction des besoins.









**Exigences** 




**Formation et expérience:** 



* Baccalauréat dans un domaine pertinent avec expérience en méthodes quantitatives;
* Capacités de programmation R : 2 ans ou plus d’expérience de niveau intermédiaire, avec une expérience pratique du tidyverse (en particulier dplyr et purrr), de l’écriture de code réutilisable et modulaire, ainsi que du développement ou de la maintenance de packages R;
* Connaissance des systèmes de contrôle de version (par exemple, git);
* Excellentes capacités d'analyse, de communication et de rédaction;
* Capacité à concevoir des visualisations de données claires, convaincantes et soignées sur le plan visuel, destinées à des publics techniques comme non techniques;
* Capacité à travailler avec du code et à suivre les meilleures pratiques de codage;
* Compréhension des principes statistiques, en particulier en ce qui concerne la conception et l'interprétation des enquêtes;
* Sens de l’organisation exceptionnel — souci du détail, capacité à mener plusieurs tâches de front et à respecter les échéances, aptitude à cerner les priorités et à gérer les attentes;
* Capacité d’adaptation : vous ne vous laissez pas déconcerter par les nouveaux défis qui se présentent à vous;
* Capacité à travailler dans un environnement au rythme rapide et à pivoter ou réagir rapidement au besoin.









**Atouts:** 



* Expérience en matière d'études de marché et/ou d'opinion publique;
* Connaissance d’autres langages et outils de programmation (par exemple SQL, Python, JavaScript, Google Apps Script); toute expérience supplémentaire en développement logiciel lié à l’analytique est un atout;
* Expérience de programmation, de lancement et de suivi de sondages programmés dans Qualtrics ou des plateformes de sondage similaires;
* Familiarité avec les flux de données basés sur AWS, notamment le stockage, l’interrogation, la transformation et l’automatisation de données à l’aide d’outils comme S3, Redshift, DynamoDB et Lambda;
* Expérience d’intégration sécuritaire de grands modèles de langage (LLM) dans des flux de travail, en particulier les outils d’assistance au code (par exemple Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI), et volonté d’intégrer de nouvelles technologies à votre travail;
* Expérience avec des outils de développement web tels que React, Next.js et CSS moderne;
* Expérience dans le domaine de la politique ou des campagnes électorales;
* Expérience de la prise de parole en public et de la présentation d'études à des publics divers;
* Bilingue (anglais et français);
* Nous travaillons à l'échelle mondiale ! La connaissance d'autres langues est appréciée.









**Ce que nous offrons** 



* Un régime d'assurance médicale et dentaire compétitif, payé à 100 % par l'employeur;
* Perkopolis: Un accès gratuit à une foule de rabais et d'économies sur les divertissements, les voyages, le magasinage et les produits de bien\\-être;
* Mode de travail hybride offrant la flexibilité du télétravail et de la collaboration au bureau;
* Des collations, du café et bien plus dans notre siège social de Montréal;
* Une tonne d'activités et de traditions pour créer un environnement inclusif et divertissant;
* Un ordinateur MacBook fourni dès ton arrivée;
* 3 semaines de vacances par année;
* 5 jours personnels à utiliser à ta discrétion;
* Un environnement de travail dynamique où aucune journée ne se ressemble;
* Des opportunités de croissance grâce au financement de cours, de conférences et de certifications;
* Un bureau moderne avec une ambiance ‘’startup’’;
* La chance de rejoindre une équipe multidisciplinaire en pleine croissance.









 La connaissance de la langue anglaise est exigée pour ce poste, car les fonctions de la personne titulaire nécessiteront des communications orales et écrites quotidiennes avec une clientèle majoritairement anglophone située à l'extérieur du Québec.

**About Us**
 What if your work could drive change in a globally established industry, shaping processes that touch every corner of the world? At Forto, we are at the forefront of change, harnessing the power of AI to revolutionise logistics. We want to reinvent digital supply chains to be transparent, frictionless and sustainable. From day one, our mission has been to simplify global trade – creating a seamless and efficient logistics process.




**Your Role \\& Mission**
 As a Data Scientist in the Data Science team at Forto, you will take ownership of production ML systems that extract structured intelligence from unstructured logistics data. You will be a Data Scientist Engineer working closely with the Engineering Manager and Product Manager across three core workstreams: document data extraction (FlashDoc), vocabulary mapping, and rate sheet parsing, while using a combination of LLMs, custom models, and rule\\-based postprocessing. Your immediate priority is ensuring continuity of existing production systems, but equally important is driving step\\-change improvements in accuracy through disruptive methods and new technologies when the opportunity arises. Beyond document automation, the team’s roadmap extends into traditional data science territory, demand forecasting, churn prediction, route optimization, and predictive analytics for logistics operations.




**What Will You Do**
* Design, build, and maintain end\\-to\\-end ML pipelines for document extraction, classification, and data enrichment in production.
* Develop and improve LLM\\-based extraction systems for complex logistics documents (packing lists, booking confirmations, invoices, rate sheets).
* Build prompt evaluation frameworks and feedback\\-based optimization loops to systematically improve extraction accuracy.
* Train custom in\\-house models using human\\-in\\-the\\-loop (HITL) data to move from assisted to fully automated extraction.
* Build and maintain semantic similarity models for free\\-text to standardized TMS vocabulary across ports, terminals, container types, legal entities, and line items.
* Contribute to rate sheet extraction: building carrier\\-specific parsing logic, postprocessing, and multi\\-file combination logic.
* Improve pipeline reliability through redesign, testing, monitoring, and alerting for non\\-deterministic ML systems.
* Evaluate and introduce disruptive approaches (new model architectures, fine\\-tuning strategies, novel evaluation methods) to achieve step\\-change accuracy improvements when incremental optimization plateaus.
* Scope and build out the team’s next generation of DS workstreams beyond document automation: demand forecasting, churn prediction, route optimization, and other predictive analytics use cases for Commercial and Logistics teams.
* Partner with Product Managers to identify where DS can solve real user pain points, proactively surface opportunities from the data, and shape product roadmaps with a data\\-informed perspective.
* Collaborate closely with Engineering teams on integration, infrastructure, and API design to ensure DS outputs are consumed reliably by downstream systems.
* Manage stakeholder expectations: communicate what is feasible given capacity, set realistic timelines, flag risks early, and negotiate prioritization trade\\-offs across teams


**Required Skills And Experience**
* 3\\+ years of professional experience in data science or machine learning engineering;
* Ability to design, deploy, and maintain ML systems in production. Go beyond model development. It includes pipeline architecture, monitoring, reliability, and handling non\\-deterministic outputs at scale;
* Ability to quickly get onboarded with new tools/ technologies/ problem space;
* Strong use of agentic tools for coding;
* Strong proficiency in Python;
* Hands\\-on experience with LLMs (prompting, fine\\-tuning, evaluation) and understanding of their limitations in production environments;
* Strong foundation in classical data science and statistics: regression, classification, time series analysis, data leakage, experimental design, and hypothesis testing;
* Strong analytical and problem\\-solving skills;
* Strong stakeholder management skills;


**Preferred Skills And Experience**
* Experience in logistics, supply chain, or freight forwarding domains;
* Experience working directly with Product Managers and Engineering teams;
* Familiarity with semantic similarity and entity resolution techniques;
* Experience with human\\-in\\-the\\-loop (HITL) workflows and designing feedback loops for model improvement;
* Experience with demand forecasting, time series modeling, or churn prediction in a business context;
* Experience with low volume data setting;
* Experience with route or network optimization (cost, risk, or profitability modeling);


 Don’t fit all of our criteria? That’s okay! We know that you might be hesitant to apply if you don’t meet all our requirements, but here at Forto, we pride ourselves on embracing diverse perspectives and celebrating potential. If you are passionate about this position and the Forto values, please apply anyway. There could be a place for you in this role – or another one that’s a perfect fit!




**Why work with us?**
 Our team is hard\\-working, constantly seeking to maximise the impact of their work, but we put our people first, always winning with care. We value efficient systems and swift, direct communication. We want everyone to have their time to speak, so that we can embrace diverse perspectives to help drive towards solutions always.

**Job Description:**  



**At DIGITALL we dont just deliver technology we deliver the future! We are explorers, knowledge\\-hunters, tech geeks, problem solvers and game changers who want to inspire and be inspired. Our DIGITALL people are always one step forward: working with top\\-notch technologies, creating innovations ahead of the market trends, sharing the passion for discovering better ways. As a human\\-centric organization, our teams are built on mutual respect and open communication, allowing everyone to be authentic, express ideas and unleash their potential. We are proud of our DIGITALL bright minds and never stop developing their skills to keep pushing boundaries together and do what we love. DIGITALL operates globally with a team of 1000 experts in 16 locations across 8 countries.**  



**Description of the position:**  



DIGITALL Nature Germany GmbH is looking for a Junior Legal Counsel to join our Legal DACH team. You will support day\\-to\\-day legal work in a technology\\-driven business, with a strong focus on commercial contracting, corporate matters, and compliance topics relevant to IT consulting and technology services.  



Working closely with business stakeholders and senior legal colleagues, you will help ensure that our internal processes and external agreements remain compliant and business\\-friendly across multiple jurisdictions in Central \\& Eastern Europe (CEE) and the DACH region (Germany, Austria, Switzerland).  



**This is your job:**  

* Draft, review, and help negotiate national and international commercial agreements in DACH (e.g., NDAs, MSA, DPA, vendor and partnership agreements);
* Prepare legal research, analyses, and practical guidance on technology\\-related laws and regulations (including data protection topics);
* Support corporate legal matters for local and international group entities in DACH (corporate governance documentation and internal procedures);
* Provide day\\-to\\-day legal support to internal stakeholders to enable business objectives while managing risk;
* Monitor legislative and regulatory developments in Germany, Austria, Switzerland, the EU, and relevant CEE/DACH jurisdictions; summarize changes and recommend actions where needed;
* Maintain accurate and well\\-structured legal documentation (contract repository, templates and compliance records) to support transparency and audit readiness;
* Participate in internal and cross\\-border projects, coordinating with external counsel when required and escalating complex issues to senior legal team members.


**Your Qualifications:**  



* 1\\. and 2\\. Staatsexamen or comparable qualifications;
* At least up to 1 year of relevant legal experience (in\\-house or law firm), preferably with exposure to commercial contracts and IT law matters;
* Good understanding of contract law and commercial law; familiarity with labour law is a plus;
* Ability to read, analyse, and summarize legal texts and translate them into practical guidance for non\\-legal stakeholders;
* Fluency in German and English;
* Strong attention to detail and ability to prioritize in a dynamic environment.


**Nice to have**  



* Experience with GDPR/privacy compliance, information security, or technology regulation;
* Experience with contract templates or contract lifecycle processes;
* Interest in IT consulting and Labour law.


**What we offer**  



* A chance to build in\\-house legal experience in a technology\\-driven, international environment;
* Mentorship and support from senior legal colleagues, with clear opportunities to grow your scope over time;
* Exposure to cross\\-border work across DACH and CEE jurisdictions;
* Working model: hybrid.


**Organizational information:**  



* All applications will be treated in strict confidentiality
* Please note that only shortlisted candidates will be invited to an interview

**About ExoClick:** 










 ExoClick is an innovative and global ad company serving 20 billion daily geo\\-targeted ads to web and mobile advertisers \\& publishers. We are part of EXOGROUP, a set of companies made up of \\+200 talents and offering a wide range of services within the digital business landscape with headquarters in Barcelona and offices in Dublin, Porto and Valencia.










**Role** 










 As a Junior Data Analyst you will be part of the Analytics team at EXOGROUP, which is a highly skilled and qualified department that has diverse responsibilities.










 Together with the Director of Analytics \\& Data Science and the Analytics team you will develop and maintain data reports that provide critical business visibility on key revenue and profit trends, by product, market, vertical and traffic sources. Additionally, you will collaborate with IT and Product teams to identify potential improvements in the platform by analysing and designing algorithms.










**Tasks** 









* Structure masses of information, identify data\\-driven trends and understand what really matters and why.
* Collect KPIs and design/define visualizations.
* Deliver insights and analytics across the company's operation and advertising departments.
* Ability to identify and escalate issues and opportunities ahead of time helping to reduce impact and improve financial / performance implications.
* Develop and maintain different internal applications and dashboards.
* Together with the Analytics team, you will develop and promote actionable insights to increase the profitability of the company.









**Skills** 









* You thrive on data and have a highly analytical mind.
* Degree in computer science or mathematical sciences.
* Managing and prioritising workload, taking ownership of all assigned tasks.
* You feel comfortable retrieving, cleaning, tidying and processing data from different sources and formats. You have a general understanding of how web applications work.
* You have programming experience in Python.
* You are familiar with SQL and Git.
* Experience with advanced statistical methodology, data and datasets is a plus.
* Strong verbal and written communication skills.
* The desire and agility to work in a fast\\-paced and ever evolving environment.









**What you'll find working at ExoClick:** 










 We offer a position in a young, dynamic and international team with exceptional working conditions in unique offices high up in the Torre Mapfre, one of Barcelona's world\\-renowned landmarks, located right on the city's seafront.




 Additionally, we offer the opportunity for permanent training, personal development, ambitious career growth, and a competitive salary.










 Most of all, we offer a position in a team that thrives on achievement, success, and leadership within our industry. Our core company value is innovation: where people and creativity drive innovative technology. If you have an innovative, winning mentality, this position is for you!










**Our company benefits:** 









* Flexitime and summer schedule;
* Private health insurance;
* Your Birthday off as a paid holiday;
* Flexible compensation plan: travel, meals \\& childcare;
* Additional internal and external training through our EXOGROUP University program;
* English, Portuguese \\& Spanish classes;
* training budget \\& study leave;
* Employee referral program bonus \\- You can earn 2500Eur by referring someone!
* Exciting team buildings in locations such as Ibiza;
* Office games room/chill\\-out zone;
* Organic fruit;
* Monday team breakfast;
* Subsidised Well\\-Being activities;
* Calm App;
* Yoga classes;
* Massages;
* Subsidized catering;
* Flexible remote work;
* Home office set up budget of 500 Eur;









 Is this not the right role for you? Then make sure to check out all other roles we have open for you on our careers website.










